---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Colophon | Denson George"
  description="How densongeorge.com was built, including its technology stack and design reference ledger."
>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="colophon-header">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>Colophon</p>
      <h1>Built deliberately.</h1>
      <p>
        The site uses an Astro static shell, a focused React and TypeScript
        island, and Fluent UI components. The visual language remains original
        to this site.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="colophon-section" aria-labelledby="colophon-stack">
      <div class="section-label">
        <span>01</span>
        <p id="colophon-stack">Technology</p>
      </div>
      <dl class="colophon-stack">
        <div>
          <dt>Astro</dt>
          <dd>
            Static HTML, routing, metadata, sitemap, and Cloudflare output.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>React + TypeScript</dt>
          <dd>
            The interactive stack explorer, isolated from the static page.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Fluent UI 9</dt>
          <dd>
            Accessible components, semantic tokens, focus behavior, and theming.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="colophon-section" aria-labelledby="reference-ledger">
      <div class="section-label">
        <span>02</span>
        <p id="reference-ledger">Reference ledger</p>
      </div>
      <div class="colophon-copy">
        <h2>Principles referenced. Expression kept original.</h2>
        <p>
          No source copy, code, illustrations, assets, measurements, or
          distinctive layouts were reused. The references below informed only
          broad design or engineering principles.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ol class="reference-list">
        <li>
          <a href="https://fluent2.microsoft.design/design-tokens">
            Fluent 2 design tokens, color, motion, and accessibility
          </a>
          <p>
            Used directly as the documented design-system foundation for the
            React island. No Microsoft brand assets or documentation copy are
            used.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://antfu.me/">Anthony Fu</a>
          <p>
            Reviewed the general principle that a technology stack can be an
            identity signal. Reinterpreted as an original, interactive workbench
            tied to this site’s actual implementation.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.joshwcomeau.com/">Josh W. Comeau</a>
          <p>
            Reviewed the broad principle that interaction can demonstrate
            technical ideas. Reinterpreted through the original agent panel and
            stack explorer; no tutorial mechanics, copy, or visual treatment
            were borrowed.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://sive.rs/now">Derek Sivers’ /now convention</a>
          <p>
            Referenced only for present-focus framing. The “current operating
            mode” copy and layout were independently written from confirmed
            facts.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://docs.astro.build/en/concepts/islands/">
            Astro islands architecture
          </a>
          <p>
            Used as the technical pattern that keeps the site static while
            hydrating only the Fluent UI experience.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="colophon-section" aria-labelledby="research-set">
      <div class="section-label">
        <span>03</span>
        <p id="research-set">Research set</p>
      </div>
      <div class="colophon-copy">
        <h2>Reviewed, not replicated.</h2>
        <p>
          Additional portfolios reviewed for contrast and quality:
          <a href="https://leerob.com/">Lee Robinson</a>,
          <a href="https://paco.me/">Paco Coursey</a>,
          <a href="https://rauno.me/">Rauno Freiberg</a>,
          <a href="https://emilkowal.ski/">Emil Kowalski</a>,
          <a href="https://delba.dev/">Delba de Oliveira</a>, and
          <a href="https://robbowen.digital/">Robb Owen</a>. Their distinctive
          copy and visual combinations were specifically excluded from this
          implementation.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
